-- title:
--   Good points lie off the other Igusa branches
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Write $k:=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and abbreviate $\mathcal M:=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field), $\mathcal F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` (the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, for $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the unit-group reduction `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`), $\mathcal M_k:=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` and $\mathcal F_k:=$ `xHFunctionFieldC k (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `Place.evalAt` is the value of an element at a place computed through the inverse of $K\to$ (residue field of the place), defined when the place is rational.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathcal M_k$ over $k$, and `hW` states that $w\in W$ precisely when $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q M' k`, i.e. $w$ is rational, satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,M')$ lies in `ssJSet q k`, the set of $j\in k$ such that every elliptic curve over $k$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero $k$-point killed by $q$.
--
--   *Reduction data.* `hle` asserts $\mathcal M\le\mathcal F$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathcal M$ to $\mathcal M_k$ over $A$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal M$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $\mathcal M_k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and its residue map, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies it with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\mathcal M$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $k$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Further, $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an element of `Idx q`).
--
--   *Igusa branches.* $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal F$ to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$. The group of hypotheses on it: `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, for $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q=[1:0]$, as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$; `hIg` states that each $\ell$ is obtained from $[1:0]$ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q=\ell$ and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is permuted by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`.
--
--   *Supersingular discs.* $O_{SS}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\mathcal F$ to each $s\in W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{SS}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular wherever the $j$-expansion `jq` is (that is, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for all places $P$ of $\mathcal M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $O_{SS}(s)$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{SS}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{SS}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{SS}(s)$ contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit of $O_{SS}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *The $\infty$-branch prolongation.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $\mathcal F$ to $\mathcal F_k$ over $A$ (valuation subring, surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$, and the scaling property), with `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O`: $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   *Uniformisers and the small field.* $\pi\in A$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$. $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ has image in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` says every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ is given, together with $\zeta_0\in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   *The level field and its model.* With $k_0$ acting on $\mathcal F$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion quantifies over all intermediate fields $F_0$ of $\mathcal F/k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\mathcal F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any finite family $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, and any $K'$-linearly independent family $c_i$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and every element of $\mathcal F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$. Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\mathcal F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. The statement further quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is the inclusion $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathcal F$, over an element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $\mathcal F$ is the $j$-expansion `jq` viewed in $\mathcal M$ and then in $\mathcal F$, with $j_1\ne 0$, and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of $\mathcal F_k$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j:\mathcal M_k\to\mathcal F_k$ such that $R$ computes $R_0$ through $j$ (for $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}$ of it is $j(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$) and such that $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ exactly when some $s\in W$ satisfies: $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in that of $Q$.
--
--   The ambient scheme is $\mathfrak X_1:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` (elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $X_{\infty}=\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` (elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` and structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$. Four local predicates are introduced. For $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart lying over $x$ there are $g,h$ in the corresponding chart algebra with $h\notin y$ and $f\,h=g$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$. For a place $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and satisfies $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f))<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of $\mathcal F_k$, says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, that $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that it lies in the nonunits of $Q$ if and only if `InMax x f`. The conclusion is stated in terms of the remaining two predicates only; `Centred`, `Reads` and the datum $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ serve to fix the common frame in which this and the neighbouring statements are phrased.
--
--   A point $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ is a good point, `GoodPt x`, when five conditions hold: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A_1$; every $y$ to which $x$ specialises equals $x$; for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every $b$ of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\mathcal F$ lies in the nonunits of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ belongs to the prime $y$; the same with $X_\infty$ and `chartAlgInf`; and for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   The predicate `OffBranch x` asserts that for every $\ell$ in the projective line with $\ell\ne\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ both of the following hold: for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ lying over $x$ there is an element $b$ of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\mathcal F$ lies in the nonunits of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not belong to the prime $y$; and for every point $y$ of $X_\infty$ lying over $x$ there is an element $b$ of `chartAlgInf` whose image in $\mathcal F$ lies in the nonunits of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and which does not belong to the prime $y$.
--
--   The assertion is: for every $x\in\mathfrak X_1$, if `GoodPt x` then `OffBranch x`.
--
--   In the Igusa-curve analysis of the reduction at $q$ of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$, this is the statement that a good closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model — one lying on the $\infty$-Igusa component and away from supersingular $j$-invariants — lies on no other Igusa branch, each of the rings $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ with $\ell\ne[1:0]$ having a nonunit that is invertible in the local ring at the point. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), which produces such points together with the place of the reduced function field they read off.
